  "query_preview": "..\nA monsoon trough extends southeastward from Typhoon Dolphin to a\npoorly-defined monsoon disturbance, newly designated Invest 98W, near\nthe far north Marianas. The monsoon trough then curves northeast \ntowards Tropical Storm Chan-Hom (previously Invest 96W) to the \ndistant northeast. An unsettled monsoon pattern dips south across the\nCNMI. A strong, squall line-like feature produced an area of \nnumerous to widespread showers and scattered thunderstorms west of \ncoastal waters earlier today, then gradually stretched eastward \nacross Rota this afternoon. Satellite trends indicated numerous \nlocally heavy showers and isolated thunderstorms training across \nRota, producing minor flooding late this afternoon and into the \nevening. Model guidance shows this feature shifting north, following \na tilt in the monsoon trough. This is expected to bring numerous \nshowers to Tinian and Saipan later this evening, capable of producing\noccasional gusts to 35 mph, and trend down to scattered showers with\nisolated thunderstorms after midnight. Several monsoon disturbance \nlinger near the far northern Marianas, this upcoming week keeping a \nwetter pattern nearby, however, there may be some lulls in the active\nweather pattern depending how convection organizes around these \nmonsoon disturbances. Some uncertainty remains since this is tied to \nthe actual location and intensity of the monsoon disturbances in the \ncoming days.",
